s-maya-archaeological-site/ | Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","when":"year-round","commission":"private Puuc day-tour extension","accessed":"2026-07-06","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"primary","expedition":"destination"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Sayil — Grand Palace (3-story, 100+ columns)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/ruta-puuc-2026-kabah-sayil-labna-uxmal-circuit.htm | Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","when":"year-round","commission":"Puuc day-tour extension","accessed":"2026-07-06","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"primary","expedition":"destination"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Labná — Arch of Labná","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/ruta-puuc-2026-kabah-sayil-labna-uxmal-circuit.htm | Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"culture","commission":"Puuc day-tour extension","accessed":"2026-07-06","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"primary","expedition":"destination"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Xlapak","tier":"premier","source":"https://en-yucatan.com/ruta-puuc/ | Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"culture","commission":"completes premium private Ruta Puuc itinerary","accessed":"2026-07-06","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"primary","expedition":"destination"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Loltún caves (700m+ guided)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://yucatantoday.com/en/lolt-n-caves/ | Accessed 2026-07-06","hook":"Uneven, sometimes slick underground surfaces over a 700m+ route; entry is guided-only for safety","si":"expedition","blurb":"Uneven, sometimes slick underground surfaces over a 700m+ route; entry is guided-only for safety","commission":"GEA add-on (guiding/transport, Host); entrance non-commissionable","accessed":"2026-07-06","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"destination","expedition":"primary"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Choco-Story México (Ecomuseo del Cacao)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://yucatantoday.com/en/blog/choco-story-uxmal-an-interactive-museum | Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"culinary","commission":"add-on ticket (affiliate/Viator) + lunch upsell","accessed":"2026-07-06","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["culinary"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"primary","culture":"destination","expedition":"destination"},"commission_lane":["affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Hacienda Yaxcopoil","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.beyondtheordinary.co.uk/features/hacienda-yaxcopoil/ | Accessed 2026-07-06","hook":"19th-C henequen estate turned atmospheric museum, on Hwy 261 en route to Uxmal; visitable and event-capable","si":"culture","blurb":"19th-C henequen estate turned atmospheric museum, on Hwy 261 en route to Uxmal; visitable and event-capable","commission":"visit add-on; private-event via Host","accessed":"2026-07-06","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"primary","expedition":"destination"},"commission_lane":["event"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Uxmal worth visiting instead of Chichén Itzá?","a":"Yes — it is the connoisseur''s Maya city. Uxmal is markedly less crowded than Chichén Itzá, with grander Puuc-style architecture: the rounded-corner Pyramid of the Magician, the lattice-stone Nunnery Quadrangle, and a Governor''s Palace whose five-acre platform carries an extended Chaac mosaic frieze. UNESCO inscribed it in 1996.","source":"mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culture","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"q":"Can you climb the pyramid at Uxmal?","a":"Partly — the distinction matters. Climbing El Adivino (the Pyramid of the Magician) is banned to protect it, but the Great Pyramid is climbable on its north side, on steep handrail-free Maya risers, so wear sturdy shoes and mind your footing. Do not assume the iconic rounded pyramid can be summited.","source":"yucatantoday.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culture","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"q":"What is the Ruta Puuc, and are the Loltún caves worth it?","a":"The Ruta Puuc is the backroad ruin circuit south of Uxmal — Kabah (whose Codz Poop wears ~250 interlocking Chaac masks), Sayil''s three-story palace, the photogenic Arch of Labná, and quiet Xlapak. The Loltún caves cap it: a 700 m+ guided-only underground walk past cave paintings and \"musical\" ringing columns. A guided day neutralizes the heat, the remote road and the mandatory cave guide in one wrapper.","source":"yucatantoday.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Uxmal and on the Puuc route?","a":"Heat and remoteness, not crime. Uxmal''s plazas are fully exposed limestone with almost no shade, and the Ruta Puuc runs long stretches with no fuel, water or medical services between sites. Time the visit for early morning or late afternoon, carry 1.5–2 L of water per person plus a hat and SPF, and leave Muna with a full tank; the nearest hospital is Mérida, ~1h15 north.","source":"yucatantoday.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety","accessed":"2026-07-06"}],"seo":{"jsonld_type":"TouristAttraction","meta_title":"Uxmal & the Ruta Puuc: UNESCO Maya City Guide (2026) | TravelWell.World","search_language":"en","local_keywords":["Uxmal Ruta Puuc","Pirámide del Adivino","espectáculo de luz y sonido Uxmal","Grutas de Loltún visita guiada","haciendas Ruta Puuc","Kabah Codz Poop"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"content_freshness":"2026-07-06","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-06","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-20T14:49:02Z","source_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}]},"long_tail":["Uxmal ruins guide 2026","Uxmal from Mérida day trip","Ruta Puuc Kabah Sayil Labná itinerary","Uxmal light and sound show tickets","Uxmal vs Chichén Itzá less crowded"]},"booking":{"advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["culture_heritage","expedition","culinary"],"ultra":[{"name":"Chablé Yucatán","tier":"ultra","earning_path":"Virtuoso / Fora","note":"#13 World''s Best Hotels 2023; 3,400+ tequila bottles; ~30 min Mérida","source":"https://www.virtuoso.com/travel/luxury-hotels/15452675/chable-yucatan | Accessed 2026-07-06"},{"name":"Hacienda Temozón (Luxury Collection)","tier":"ultra","earning_path":"Virtuoso / Marriott STARS / Fora / MoR","note":"28 rooms; ~35 min Uxmal — natural Puuc base","source":"https://www.travelweekly.com/Hotels/Abala-Mexico/Hacienda-Temozon-Luxury-Collection-p51093491 | Accessed 2026-07-06"},{"name":"Hacienda Santa Rosa (Luxury Collection)","tier":"ultra","earning_path":"Virtuoso / Marriott STARS / MoR","note":"intimate 11 rooms","source":"https://www.letstraveltomexico.com/yucatan-haciendas/ | Accessed 2026-07-06"},{"name":"The Lodge at Uxmal","tier":"premier","earning_path":"Host FIT / MoR","note":"on-gate, walk to ruins"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Uxmal, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":20.3597,"lng":-89.7714},"orbit":[{"id":"celestun-mexico","jewels":6,"si":["expedition","tropical"]},{"id":"chichen-itza-mexico","jewels":7,"si":["culture","expedition","wellness"]},{"id":"izamal-mexico","jewels":8,"si":["culture","romance","culinary"]},{"id":"merida-mexico","jewels":15,"si":["romance","expedition","culture","culinary"]},{"id":"rio-lagartos-mexico","jewels":6,"si":["expedition","tropical"]},{"id":"valladolid-mexico","jewels":9,"si":["expedition","culture","culinary"]}],"orbit_country":["akumal-mexico","bacalar-mexico","balandra-beach-mexico","cabo-pulmo-mexico","cabo-san-lucas-mexico","calakmul-mexico","campeche-city-mexico","cancun-mexico","careyes-mexico","chapala-ajijic-mexico","coba-mexico","costalegre-mexico","cozumel-mexico","east-cape-mexico","ensenada-mexico","espiritu-santo-island-mexico","guadalajara-mexico","guanajuato-city-mexico","holbox-mexico","huatulco-mexico","isla-contoy-mexico","isla-mujeres-mexico","la-paz-mexico","loreto-mexico","los-barriles-mexico","magdalena-bay-mexico","mahahual-mexico","mazamitla-mexico","mexico-city-mexico","oaxaca-city-mexico","palenque-mexico","playa-del-carmen-mexico","puerto-aventuras-mexico","puerto-morelos-mexico","puerto-vallarta-mexico","punta-mita-mexico","san-cristobal-de-las-casas-mexico","san-jose-del-cabo-mexico","san-miguel-de-allende-mexico","san-sebastian-del-oeste-mexico","sayulita-mexico","sian-kaan-mexico","teotihuacan-mexico","tlaquepaque-mexico","todos-santos-mexico","tulum-mexico","valle-de-guadalupe-mexico","puerto-escondido-mexico"]}'::jsonb, 125),
  ('valladolid-mexico', '10S', 'Valladolid', 'Mexico', 'Valladolid Yucatán', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Yucatán (Mérida & Chichén Itzá)', '{"expedition","culture","culinary"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["1543 colonial city + Pueblo Magico (2012), ~150 km from both Merida and Cancun; mid-peninsula base","Cenote Zaci in the heart of town (short staircase, park); swimmable, free w/ ~100 MXN restaurant","Cenote Suytun ~5 km E - iconic single light-beam on stone platform ~1-3 PM; ~250 MXN (230 online), 9 AM-5 PM","Cenote Oxman on a working hacienda - deep sinkhole + roots + rope swing + pool; 150 MXN (350 w/ lunch)","Ek Balam ~30 min N - CLIMBABLE 32 m acropolis (unlike Chichen), intricate stucco; ~170 MXN cash only"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"basic hospitals in town; nearest full trauma care Merida (~2 hr W, Star Medica/Clinica de Merida) or Cancun (~2 hr E, Hospiten/Amerimed) or air-evac","air_access_verified":"yes - ~2 hr from MID Merida and ~2 hr from CUN Cancun (~150 km from each)","heat":"intense Yucatan sun - visit cenotes/Ek Balam at 9 AM opening; carry water + SPF; heat exhaustion risk at open ruins","cenote":"Zaci/Suytun/Oxman = swim/snorkel, NO lifeguard; life jackets (mandatory posture for non-swimmers/children); shower off sunscreen; slick platforms (Suytun) + rope swing (Oxman) - jump only where directed","dive_spine":"DISTINGUISH swim/snorkel (no cert) vs GUIDED cavern dive (certified cavern guide, light zone) vs CAVE dive (TECHNICAL - full cave cert, overhead, silt-out - FLAG HARD, never blur). Yucatan = world''s longest flooded caves (Ox-Bel-Ha ~269 km)","hyperbaric_no_fly":"nearest chambers on coast ~2+ hr (SSS/DAN Cancun, Playa, Cozumel; SSS Merida ~2 hr W); interior Yucatan has NO adjacent chamber - multi-hour evac for cave/cavern diving; DAN = nearest hospital first; observe no-fly 18-24 hr after multi-day/repetitive dives; carry DAN insurance","malaria":"effectively none in tourist zone","dengue":"active in Yucatan 2026; chikungunya/Zika circulate - use repellent","water":"bottled/purified only","hurricane":"Jun-Nov","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-09-04T12:02:56Z","page_updated":"2026-09-04T00:25:51+01:00","source_country":"mexico","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely","fcdo_zones":[{"name":"The city of Tijuana, in Baja California","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["airside transit through Tijuana airport","the Cross Border Xpress bridge linking the airport across the border","federal toll road 1D and the Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border"]},{"name":"The city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"The state of Chihuahua","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Chihuahua","the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez via federal toll road 45","federal toll road 45D between Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez","the Copper Canyon rail route and the towns immediately on it, including Creel","the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro","state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua"],"note":"The advisory also covers the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"name":"The state of Sinaloa","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán","road 32 between El Fuerte and Los Mochis","the 15D federal toll road running the length of the state","the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis and El Fuerte, and the towns immediately on it"]},{"name":"The state of Tamaulipas","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo via federal toll road 85D from Monterrey","federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad Victoria and Magueyes","the area of Tamaulipas south of those highways"]},{"name":"The state of Zacatecas","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"In Guanajuato: the areas south-west of road 45D","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D. (San Miguel de Allende and Guanajuato City sit outside this area.)"},{"name":"The state of Michoacán","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Morelia via federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43","toll road 48D between Morelia and its airport","the town of Pátzcuaro via toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips on Lake Pátzcuaro","Federal Highway 15D"]},{"name":"In Jalisco: the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the Colima border","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Thirty-nine named municipalities, including Autlán de Navarro, Sayula, Tapalpa, Cocula and Villa Corona — the advisory lists each by name."},{"name":"In Jalisco: eleven northern municipalities","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Bolaños, Chimaltitán, Colotlán, Hostotipaquillo, Huejúcar, Huequilla el Alto, Mezquitic, San Martín de Bolaños, Santa María de los Ángeles, Totatiche and Villa Guerrero."},{"name":"The state of Colima","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Manzanillo by sea, or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport","direct travel via road 200 from that airport to Manzanillo"]},{"name":"The state of Guerrero, including the city of Acapulco","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air"]},{"name":"Within 40km of the Guatemalan border, from the Pacific Coast up to and including the Gracias a Dios crossing","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"Federal Highway 199 between Rancho Nuevo, outside San Cristóbal de las Casas, and the Chancalá junction outside Palenque","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"The restriction is the highway segment, not the towns at either end."}]},"timi