fe","si_map_basis":"nightlife retired and folded back into Global Live Entertainment — David 2026-08-23","source":"https://onehappyisland.com/palm-beach-aruba/","accessed":"2026-07-30","source_carried":true,"source_basis":"carried from the dossier lane source; the proper noun ''Palm Beach'' from the jewel name appears in the URL. NOT a human read of the jewel.","si_fold_note":"folded from the retired `nightlife` slug into Global Live Entertainment 2026-08-23; the content is kept, the retired slug is not"},{"name":"The Aruban table","status":"future","tier":"essential","price_band":"~$25-150/pp","timing":"Dec-Apr","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"keshi yena, fresh fish and food-truck culture, plus a strong Palm Beach/Oranjestad restaurant scene — a Dutch-Caribbean plate with range","si":"culinary","blurb":"keshi yena, fresh fish and food-truck culture, plus a strong Palm Beach/Oranjestad restaurant scene — a Dutch-Caribbean plate with range","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"venue/bundle","wells":["eat"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culinary","tropical"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culinary":"primary","diveglobal":"destination","entertainment":"destination","ocean":"destination","romance":"destination","tropical":"evidenced"},"commission_lane":["venue","bundle"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Aruba?","a":"Not storms or crime - small stuff. Aruba is south of the hurricane belt (very low storm risk) and low-crime, so plan for petty theft, strong sun and dengue, plus no-fly 18-24h if you dive the Antilla. It''s about as low-stress as Caribbean travel gets.","source":"onehappyisland.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"When is the best time to go to Aruba?","a":"Year-round - Aruba is warm, dry and reliably sunny with no real storm season. December-April is peak (winter escape, highest prices); May-August is warm, quieter value and windiest (best for windsurf and Hi-Winds).","source":"onehappyisland.com","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Which beach - Eagle or Palm?","a":"Both: Eagle Beach for the wide, quiet, top-rated sand and fofoti trees; Palm Beach for the resort strip, watersports and nightlife. Most people beach at Eagle and stay at Palm.","source":"onehappyisland.com","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Do I need to be a diver to see the Antilla wreck?","a":"No - the water is so clear that snorkelers can see the 400-ft wreck from the surface in ~60ft, and most excursions include boat, snorkel gear and guiding. Certified divers penetrate deeper sections (advanced); everyone else snorkels the shallows (no no-fly restriction).","source":"visitaruba.com","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Is Aruba good for windsurfing or a wildlife day?","a":"Both are signatures. Hadicurari (Fisherman''s Huts) is a world-class windsurf/kite beach (Hi-Winds each June/July), and you can wade with flamingos on Renaissance Island or hike Arikok National Park to the Natural Pool - beyond the beach, Aruba has real range.","source":"aruba.com","si_tag":"ocean"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Aruba Travel Guide: Eagle & Palm Beach, the Antilla Wreck, Arikok & Windsurfing","meta_description":"Plan Aruba - the Caribbean''s sure-thing sun, safely south of the hurricane belt: top-rated Eagle Beach, the 400-ft Antilla wreck (snorkelable), world-class Hadicurari windsurfing, Arikok National Park and the Natural Pool, and the flamingos of Renaissance Island.","slug":"aruba","primary_keyword":"Aruba travel guide","long_tail":["Eagle Beach Aruba","Antilla wreck dive snorkel","Aruba Hi-Winds windsurfing Hadicurari","Arikok National Park Natural Pool","Renaissance Island flamingos","is Aruba safe"],"search_language":"nl","local_keywords":["Aruba","One Happy Island","Eagle Beach","Palm Beach","Antilla","Hadicurari","Arikok","Conchi","Oranjestad","flamingo"],"hreflang":["en","nl"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_fr